   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "### Split a character into parts (Qwen Image 2.1)\n\nLoad the **full character image** once. Each row crops one part with **Image Crop** and isolates it with a Qwen Image 2.1 edit.\n\n**Image Crop** = `width`, `height`, `x`, `y` in pixels of the source (top-left is 0, 0). The boxes fit the example `source_cyclops.png` (1664 × 2480). For your own character, read the box from your image (hover in any image viewer) and leave a generous margin.\n\n**Rule:** each part brings what hides its seam: the whole beard for the head, the wrap for arms and legs. One arm and one leg are enough, mirror them in Blender.\n\nSeed 56 fixed, 25 steps, cfg 1, euler / simple. Body at 1536, parts at 1024. Mute a row (Ctrl+M) to skip a part."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
